WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.700
Our World leader.

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.502
Today marks one week

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.471
since Russia dusted off its Cold

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.739
War playbook and detained

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.639
American journalist

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.475
Evan Jurkovec

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.011
and accused him falsely of espionage.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.611
It's a charge

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.780
that is, by all accounts, completely

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.248
make believe.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:15.982
A week later,

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:16.416
the Wall Street

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.017
Journal reporter

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.019
has yet to even get consular access

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.520
or meet with American officials.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.121
Secretary of State

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:24.190
Antony Blinken today said this.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.192
In my own mind, there's no doubt

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.561
that he's being wrongfully detained

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.229
by Russia,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.363
which is exactly what I said

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.464
to Foreign Minister Lavrov

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.966
when I spoke to him

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:36.002
over the weekend and insisted

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.638
that Evan be released immediately.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.173
Joining us now, retired

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.408
journalist Nicholas Daniloff.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.610
He was Moscow bureau chief for U.S.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.678
News and World Report in 1986

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.881
when he was falsely arrested

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.848
and wrongfully detained

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.283
in a KGB prison

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.951
for 13 days, falsely

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.553
accused of being a spy.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.321
Thanks so much for joining us.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.890
Secretary Blinken says the U.S.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.258
is still preparing

00:00:58.258 --> 00:00:59.526
to officially declare

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.660
this a wrongful detention,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.395
which would trigger new U.S.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.531
government resources to work toward

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.266
his release. It's been a week.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.967
Is the Biden administration working

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.035
quickly enough here?

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:11.971
Well, the fact that

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:12.872
Biden's name

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.874
has been attached to all of this

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.843
strikes me as important

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.645
and that the secretary of state

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.180
is also involved.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.849
So something is going on.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.918
When the Russians falsely

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.287
accused you of being a spy,

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.722
did they even bother to try to come up

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.558
with any sort of junk evidence

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.525
to use against you?

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:32.792
Or did

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.429
they just make the claim and lock you up?

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.832
They made the claim and locked me up.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.266
You were detained

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.935
just days after an employee

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:42.602
of the Soviet

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.237
Union's mission to the United Nations

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.406
had been arrested in New York.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:46.940
And both you

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.141
and that employee were released

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.275
after two weeks

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.344
of diplomatic negotiations.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.446
Why do you think Russia,

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:53.980
for the first time

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.348
since the Cold War, is now detaining

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.517
this, detaining this American journalist,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.219
accusing him of espionage?

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:02.122
Do you think it's the same basic idea?

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.357
A Russian spy was arrested.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:04.891
Therefore,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.392
they took this American journalist

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.794
and they just want to do a swap, as

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.928
seemed to be the case with you,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.799
that that may well be the case.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.267
I think that

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:18.004
bureaucracy is, you know, remain in place

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.273
and they are often guided

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.642
by the practice of the past.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:25.311
So if this seems like

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.113
a throwback to the past,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.915
it probably is Gursky,

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:29.782
which is being detained

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.384
in the same center

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.418
where they detained you

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.753
in 1986, a place

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.288
that has a long, intimidating history

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.191
that dates back to Stalin's purges.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.392
If ever everyone could hear you

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.860
right now.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.061
What would be your message

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:45.331
or advice to him as he sits essentially

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:49.035
in the same place you sat?

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.405
Well, when I was in that prison,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.375
the one thing that I did not have

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.209
any access

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.312
to was information from the outside side.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.181
I got information

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.149
from visits from my wife.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.317
And so I think

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.852
one of the things that he could do

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.820
is demand

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.223
to be informed about what's going on

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.925
in the outside world.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:14.594
And they probably won't comply with that.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.229
But you make the demand anyway.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:17.697
Do you

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.498
think there's anything

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:22.068
to the fact that both you and Evan

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.238
are of Russian descent,

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.874
that that might be behind

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.176
why they did this?

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.413
I would think that

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:36.182
that is not much of a connection.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.551
In my case,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.820
the Russian connection was helpful

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.055
in that

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.356
I could get on

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.525
with the people surrounding me.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.596
I could speak with them in Russian,

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:54.000
and that created a somewhat

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.336
more friendly atmosphere

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.104
within the prison.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.572
You were released, thankfully,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.174
after 13 days of detention.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.408
This was while

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.277
Mikhail Gorbachev was president

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.346
of the Soviet Union.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.847
Given that we're dealing with Vladimir

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:08.448
Putin here,

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.583
who seems a much more

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.985
nefarious individual

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.821
than Mikhail Gorbachev, perhaps.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.822
Are you worried at all

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.190
the girls Djokovic's story

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.524
will not end as quickly

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.728
or as smoothly as yours did?

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.463
It may not.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.430
It may not.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.699
Because for the very reason that

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.134
that you mentioned.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.503
All right, Nick Daniloff, it's

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.771
been an honor talking to you, sir.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.505
Thank you so much.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.173
Really appreciate it.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.476
Well, it's a pleasant

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.077
being on your program.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.445
Thank you, sir. Have a good day.

